WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.925
- [Woman] And it was

00:00:00.925 --> 00:00:03.203
you regularly say that 
failure propels you,

00:00:03.203 --> 00:00:05.172
are there any 
instances in your past

00:00:05.172 --> 00:00:08.308
truly where you couldn't 
get over it and why?

00:00:08.308 --> 00:00:11.044
- Nope.
(audience laughter)

00:00:14.952 --> 00:00:16.650
By the way, by the way,

00:00:16.650 --> 00:00:19.653
that's the same answer for
everybody in this room.

00:00:19.653 --> 00:00:21.321
That's what humans are good at.

00:00:21.321 --> 00:00:22.623
We all fail.

00:00:22.623 --> 00:00:24.510
We've all failed.

00:00:26.661 --> 00:00:28.595
My parents haven't been killed.

00:00:28.595 --> 00:00:32.232
My child, I mean, there's people
that have their children die.

00:00:32.232 --> 00:00:34.434
Could you imagine?

00:00:34.434 --> 00:00:36.079
The shit I deal,

00:00:36.079 --> 00:00:38.038
listen, unfortunately 
or fortunately

00:00:38.038 --> 00:00:40.007
depends on how one 
wants to look at it,

00:00:40.007 --> 00:00:41.208
I'm a pretty optimistic guy,

00:00:41.208 --> 00:00:44.570
I lost three of my four
grandparents before I knew them.

00:00:44.570 --> 00:00:47.281
Two before I was born 
and one very early on.

00:00:47.281 --> 00:00:50.517
So it's easy for me to be happy.

00:00:50.517 --> 00:00:53.520
I have my shit 
in the right order.

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:55.856
The health and 
well-being of my family.

00:00:55.856 --> 00:00:59.259
And there's nothing even
remotely close to that.

00:00:59.259 --> 00:01:01.228
Not even remote,
not even remotely.

00:01:01.228 --> 00:01:03.730
People have gotten 
through much worse.

00:01:03.730 --> 00:01:05.866
This why I'm trying to 
recall our grandparents

00:01:05.866 --> 00:01:07.367
and our great-grandparents.

00:01:07.367 --> 00:01:10.485
People were 
persecuted and killed.

00:01:10.485 --> 00:01:12.606
We do not have real headaches.

00:01:12.606 --> 00:01:15.409
You know, I don't know 
why I have this

00:01:15.409 --> 00:01:17.010
highly emotional and then

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:18.946
completely unemotional 
part of me

00:01:18.946 --> 00:01:21.315
but I mix them together 
to create the balance

00:01:21.315 --> 00:01:22.559
and that's what works for me.

00:01:22.559 --> 00:01:26.453
Of course there's nothing 
that I couldn't get up from.

00:01:26.453 --> 00:01:28.689
Like every other 
human ever besides

00:01:28.689 --> 00:01:30.057
somebody who now lives in some

00:01:30.057 --> 00:01:32.695
weird cave that 
we don't know about.

00:01:32.695 --> 00:01:33.927
You know what I mean?
- [Woman] I do.

00:01:33.927 --> 00:01:36.330
- We are strong as shit.

00:01:36.330 --> 00:01:38.098
We're really fucking strong,

00:01:38.098 --> 00:01:40.400
we're just being 
sold that we're not

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:42.402
'cause there's a lot of money,

00:01:42.402 --> 00:01:44.438
a lot of money 
in telling us that

00:01:44.438 --> 00:01:47.307
we're not pretty enough,
thin enough,

00:01:47.307 --> 00:01:49.943
smart enough,
good enough.

00:01:49.943 --> 00:01:50.836
Fuck that.

00:01:50.836 --> 00:01:52.946
I want to tell you you're the
fucking best, go do shit.

00:01:52.946 --> 00:01:56.586
(audience cheers and applause)

00:02:03.916 --> 00:02:06.653
- I don't think you can end on a
higher note than fuck that.

00:02:06.653 --> 00:02:08.428
(audience laughter)

00:02:08.428 --> 00:02:09.795
- It was actually do shit.

